# Project Results and Reports
results/*
!results/combined_bpb_vs_static.json
!results/leaderboard.json
!results/domain_transfer/
!results/domain_transfer/*.json
!results/token_gain/
!results/token_gain/*.json
!results/token_gain_bpb/
!results/token_gain_bpb/*.json
!results/gsm8k/
!results/gsm8k/**
!results/hellaswag/
!results/hellaswag/**
!results/mmlu_pro_1k/
!results/mmlu_pro_1k/**
# The E9 re-score's per-example samples are 2.9 GB (17 models, and the hf backend logs far more
# per hellaswag item than July's vLLM did), against 383 MB for the whole July column. They are
# archived to $WORK/e9_column_samples/ -- $WORK, not $SCRATCH, because $SCRATCH is purged ~40d --
# and deliberately NOT tracked. results_*.json and gen_audit.json carry every number the docs
# quote; the samples are evidence for one-off forensics (they are what diagnosed gemma-4-12B).
results/gsm8k/**/samples_*.jsonl
results/hellaswag/**/samples_*.jsonl
results/mmlu_pro_1k/**/samples_*.jsonl
# The superseded July column, moved here by tools/collect_e9.py. The preregistration requires the
# July answer to be reported ALONGSIDE the new one as the superseded result, so its raw logs must
# stay in the repo -- without this the move would silently drop them, since results/* is ignored.
!results/legacy_july_bench/
!results/legacy_july_bench/**
!results/alignment_matrix.json
!results/math_domain_benchmark_analysis.json
# E2's analysis output and the aggregate harness JSON it is computed from. docs/PROGRESS.md and
# docs/RUN_LEDGER.md quote these numbers, so a clone has to be able to grep them.
# Written as an ALLOWLIST on purpose: un-ignoring the tree wholesale pulls in 3.6 GB of
# samples_*.jsonl, which is the same near-miss that put train_state/ in here. Per-example samples
# live in gs://gpu-llm-training-gceval/token_gain/adapted_bench/ and stay there.
!results/adapted_benchmark_analysis.json
!results/e2_confound_audit.json
!results/pairwise_significance.json
!results/tokenizer_bias_ext.json
!results/seed_sensitivity.json
# The criterion's own paired item-bootstrap intervals, and the two-candidate decision rule computed
# from them. Both are READ by gates, not just quoted: make_mechanism_table.py --check crashes
# without criterion_uncertainty.json, analyze_decision_rule.py reads it, and verify_paper_numbers.py
# asserts 26 prose numbers against the pair. Fourth time an artifact has shipped without its
# allowlist line; the defect is invisible in place and only a fresh clone shows it.
!results/criterion_uncertainty.json
!results/decision_rule.json
# E10: the late-position control. The raw per-position cells are ~2 MB each and stay in
# $SCRATCH/e10_late_position; only the analysis lands here.
!results/late_position.json
# E11: the downstream fine-tune. Task data (2,500 articles) stays in $SCRATCH/e11_downstream;
# the manifest and the verdict land here.
!results/downstream.json
!results/downstream_task.json
# E12: the non-generative downstream task (in-domain multiple choice). Task data (2,500 questions)
# stays in $SCRATCH/e12_mcq; the manifest and the verdict land here.
!results/mcq.json
!results/mcq_task.json

# The council/review docs the state files CITE by path. results/* is an allowlist, so without
# these three the citations in docs/PLAN.md, docs/PROGRESS.md and docs/RUN_LEDGER.md resolve to
# nothing in a fresh clone -- the same defect class that broke the 2026-08-30 release. The raw
# per-engine dumps stay untracked on purpose: they are unverified LEADS, and only the adjudicated
# and actioned documents belong in the repo.
!results/_council/
results/_council/*
!results/_council/ADJUDICATION.md
!results/_council/e8_review.txt
!results/_council/e8_gate_review.md
!results/_council/framing_ADJUDICATION.md
!results/_council/framing_question.txt
!results/_council/framing_claude_own.md
# The divergence analysis behind the paper's motivating pair, and the artifact that records why the
# gap-size correlation is NOT reported as an estimate. Added 2026-08-30: the tool shipped without
# this line, so `make check` passed locally off an untracked file and would have failed in CI on a
# fresh clone -- caught by running the gate inside a clean checkout, not by running it here.
!results/selection_divergence.json
# E4: the in-domain cloze scores and the validity analysis computed from them. The per-model files
# carry their per-item generations (~540 KB each, 6 MB total) and are committed deliberately -- the
# whole point of a generation-scored criterion is that a reader can audit what was actually
# produced, which a summary accuracy does not let them do.
!results/cloze/
!results/cloze/*.json
!results/cloze_validity.json
# E5: the mathematics criterion and the 2x2 computed from it, same reasoning (4.4 MB). Added
# because the E4 block above did NOT cover a second results directory -- verified with
# `git add -n results/cloze_math/`, never with `git check-ignore`, whose exit code is misleading
# for negated patterns and which is how a public release shipped without its evidence in August.
!results/cloze_math/
!results/cloze_math/*.json
!results/cloze_steering.json
!results/cloze_reddit/
!results/cloze_reddit/*.json
!results/cloze_hackernews/
!results/cloze_hackernews/*.json
!results/cloze_coverage.json
# Two small artifacts that docs/RUN_LEDGER.md cites BY PATH and quotes numbers from. Both existed
# only locally until 2026-09-10, so those citations resolved to nothing in a fresh clone -- found
# by tools/repo_map.py running inside a clean checkout, which is the fourth occurrence of this
# allowlist defect class. contamination_summary.json is committed despite its miscalibrated
# "CRITICAL" label (the ledger explains why the label is wrong and what the operational facts are);
# hiding the file did not stop a reader encountering the claim, it only stopped them auditing it.
!results/sensitivity_gemma12b.json
!results/contamination/
results/contamination/*
!results/contamination/contamination_summary.json

# The tier-mechanism artifact carries the paper's EXPLANATION for demoting the free tier
# (results/tier_mechanism.json). Caught missing by cloning into a temp dir and running the
# gates there -- `git add -n` in the working copy is necessary but not sufficient, because
# an untracked-but-present file passes every check run in place.
!results/tier_mechanism.json
# E3 cohort extension: the six new models' BPB and cloze cells, and the pooled analysis.
!results/cohort_ext/
!results/cohort_ext/**/*.json
!results/cohort_extension.json
# The base config of an EXCLUDED model, kept because paper_sota.tex Sec. sec:adaptedacc quotes its
# head_dim / global_head_dim as the reason the exclusion could not be waived. A claim in the paper
# has to cite something a reader can grep.
!results/model_configs/
!results/model_configs/*.json
!results/adapted_bench/
results/adapted_bench/**
!results/adapted_bench/**/
!results/adapted_bench/**/results_*.json
!results/adapted_bench/**/*_table.json
!results/adapted_bench/bpb/*.json
# The superseded HPO sweep's search records only -- these are the evidence for the
# fixed-configuration decision argued in paper_sota.tex Sec. 3.2 (4 completed trials for the
# largest models against 17-18 for the smallest). Checkpoints stay excluded by the
# final_checkpoint/best_checkpoint rules below.
!results/legacy_sweep/
!results/legacy_sweep/*/
!results/legacy_sweep/*/trials.csv
!results/legacy_sweep/*/best_config.json
!results/legacy_sweep/*/sweep_meta.json
!results/legacy_sweep/*/result_*.json
!results/legacy_sweep/*/suspicious_indices.json
!results/legacy_sweep/README.md
# ...but not the bulky rendered reports: reports/11-model-run/ already publishes
# that same legacy run's HTML/PDF/plots, and a second copy is 5 MB of duplication.
results/legacy_sweep/report.*
results/legacy_sweep/summary*.json
results/legacy_sweep/run.log
results_*/
reports/*
!reports/11-model-run/
!reports/11-model-run/**
logs/
*.log

